seo_description: "Access 40+ of the world's leading photo agencies through one account. Editorial, celebrity, sports and exclusive paparazzi, licensed for LatAm media buyers."
permalink: /licensing/
lang: en
faq:
  - question: "What is editorial image licensing?"
    answer: "Editorial licensing covers the use of photography in news, media, and informational contexts — print and digital publications, broadcasters, and social media with a journalistic or informational purpose. All content licensed through Grosby Group is cleared for editorial use across Latin America and the US Hispanic market."
  - question: "What is the difference between editorial and commercial licensing?"
    answer: "Editorial licensing covers use in news, media, and informational contexts. Commercial licensing covers advertising and promotional use. All content licensed through Grosby Group for LatAm publishers and creators is cleared for editorial and social media use. Contact us if you have a commercial use case."
  - question: "Can I license images for multiple publications under one account?"
    answer: "Yes. Many of our publisher clients operate multiple titles. We structure accounts to cover your full publication portfolio — contact us to discuss the right arrangement for your group."
  - question: "How is Grosby different from Getty Images?"
    answer: "Grosby is a boutique agency, not a platform. We represent 40+ specialist agencies — including exclusive paparazzi content Getty deliberately avoids — and provide direct account management. You deal with a named person who knows your market, not a search box."
  - question: "Which agencies does Grosby represent?"
    answer: "We represent 40+ of the world's leading editorial agencies including AFP, Mega Agency, Splash by Shutterstock, Backgrid, Alamy, Imago, Sipa, Zuma Press, Camera Press, and many more. See the full list at /partners/."
  - question: "How quickly can I get images for a breaking story?"
    answer: "Our team monitors breaking news around the clock. For urgent editorial needs, contact us directly and we will prioritise your request. Established account holders can download from the archive platform immediately."
